  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a direct relationship between Npc191948 and Prelamin-A/C, mediated through Ataxin-2. Multiple paths indicate that Npc191948 targets Ataxin-2, which in turn is a target of various compounds, including 5-Oxobrucine and 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol. These compounds are all implicated in targeting Prelamin-A/C, suggesting a common mechanism of action that involves Ataxin-2 as a central node. The consistent scores across the paths indicate a robust, albeit indirect, connection between Npc191948 and Prelamin-A/C, likely through the activation of Ataxin-2. The evidence supports a pathway where Npc191948 influences Ataxin-2, which then interacts with other molecules that ultimately affect Prelamin-A/C. This integration highlights the role of Ataxin-2 as a critical intermediary in the relationship between Npc191948 and Prelamin-A/C.",
